PROJECT YamlCheck   (a console tool that shows how a parser reads your YAML)

CREATE a console project; add the YamlDotNet package.

PROGRAM
  EXPECT one argument: the path to a YAML file
  LOAD the file into a YAML stream
    ON syntax error: PRINT line, column, message; EXIT 1
  FOR EACH document in the stream
    CONVERT the root node to JSON
    PRINT it indented

CONVERT node
  mapping   -> JSON object (keys are the key text)
  sequence  -> JSON array
  scalar    -> see SCALAR RULES

SCALAR RULES  (YAML 1.2 core schema)
  quoted ('..' or "..") or block (| or >)  -> string, always
  empty, ~, null                           -> null
  true / false (any case)                  -> boolean
  looks like an integer                    -> number
  looks like a decimal or 1e3              -> number
  anything else                            -> string

RUN
  dotnet run --project YamlCheck -- ../broken.yaml

NOTE
  JSON shows types plainly: strings in quotes, numbers and booleans without.
  That is the whole point of the tool.
